# Three territories with a biome each, a command that touches none of them.
#
# **`spec/planet.md`: *Each territory has a biome*, and *a biome earns its place by being shown
# rather than by being obeyed.*** So what there is to assert is that a terrain can be stated and
# that nothing a rule does disturbs it - which is *shown rather than obeyed* said as a test.
#
# **`terrain` is the join and `biome` is the vocabulary.** `spec/data/schema.4x` says it in those
# words: *`biome` is vocabulary and `terrain` is state, which is why only the second carries a
# `{state}` row - the six do not change while a game runs, and which territory has which is the
# world.*
#
# **Three biomes and not six, which is a limitation rather than a choice.** The mutation sweep
# found all six biome rows with nothing referring to any of them - `C-218` - so the test this
# wanted to be names all six. **A fourth `{terrain}` row is refused** with *`terrain`.`of` is
# `territory-4`, and no `territory` has that key*, though `{territory id:4 name:territory-4}` is
# declared above it; four territories with three terrains pass. **`S-247` carries the four
# measurements.** Three of the six rows become load-bearing here and the other three wait on that.
#
# **The command is a refresh because it has to fire and must not be about terrain.** A test where
# nothing happens would pass against an engine that cannot run at all; this moves a scout's
# `moving` and leaves every terrain alone, so the `{then}` asserts rather than copies.

{test name:a-territorys-biome-is-not-changed-by-a-rule}

{given}
{territory id:1 name:territory-1}
{territory id:2 name:territory-2}
{territory id:3 name:territory-3}
{place id:1 of:territory-1 layer:surface name:place-1}
{terrain of:territory-1 is:ocean}
{terrain of:territory-2 is:ice}
{terrain of:territory-3 is:desert}
{scout where:place-1 moving:0} -> 1

{when}
{refresh what:unit trait:moving}

{then}
{territory id:1 name:territory-1}
{territory id:2 name:territory-2}
{territory id:3 name:territory-3}
{place id:1 of:territory-1 layer:surface name:place-1}
{terrain of:territory-1 is:ocean}
{terrain of:territory-2 is:ice}
{terrain of:territory-3 is:desert}
{scout where:place-1 moving:1} -> 1
